# A unit-level constant built by a type another unit declares is a
# construction, which a unit-level constant cannot hold -- refused as the same
# construction of a type of this unit is.
#
# It was accepted when the path's ROOT named a unit: `json.Value 5` read as an
# application of the unit `json`, and the constant's uses reached the emitter
# untyped (E0500 "unhandled callee"). Usually the argument is a stray word: the
# next line's `main` after `json.Value`.
Value: json.Value 5

main: function is {
    v: Value.text "boxed".string
    print (json.serialize :v)
}
